# Runtime state lives in the user's XDG dirs, not the source tree
# (see internal/paths): instances + tier keys under $XDG_DATA_HOME/cs-sandbox,
# the firecracker cache under $XDG_CACHE_HOME/cs-sandbox. Nothing mutable here.

# Go build output
/bin/

# goreleaser release artifacts
/dist/

# Local credentials and env config
/.env

# Coverage data. Every test target writes a tier directory here; the merged
# profile and report are derived from them. The baseline (.coverage-baseline)
# is committed on purpose — it is what makes a lost suite reviewable.
.coverage/

# A local cross-repo workspace is a personal dev tool, never committed:
# it would override the go.mod pins for anyone who cloned this.
go.work
go.work.sum

# Diagnostics the proxied agent tiers keep past the run that made them: the
# recorder's whole log, and the requests a replay could not serve. Outside the
# test's own temp dir on purpose, because a diagnostic that goes away with the
# test answers nothing. The cassettes under test/ are committed; these are not.
/.tmp/
